; Applied by every build: this is translation rather than a change to what the
; game does, unlike the panel-every-round feature it shared a file with until
; the two were told apart -- features/enemy-panel/, the folder that whole
; feature lives in.
;
; It resolves CardEnglishLabel and 表示種族 by name, from patches/card_names.jaf
; and the generated build/race_names.jaf, so alice-tools has to be handed both
; of those before this file or it stops with "Unable to resolve function".
;
; Save this file as UTF-8 with no BOM. The assembler reads a byte order mark as
; an instruction and stops on line 1 -- "Invalid instruction: ϻ" -- and an
; editor that defaults .jam to UTF-8-with-BOM will quietly put one back.
;
; The two card Ids on the panel -- the card the enemy is captured as, and the
; one it can be stolen from -- in English.
;
; EnemyInformationView@SetParam writes them straight out:
;
;   label("Capture").SetText(g_battleContext.Capture.CaptureTarget)
;   label("Steal").SetText(g_battleContext.Capture.StealTarget)
;
; and what those two getters return is a card Id rather than a name. It is the
; key CardGenerator@GenerateFromId builds the captured card from, the one
; CardCapture@GetTreasureBoxCardIds puts in the chest, the one IsCaptureSuccess
; compares against "", and CaptureTarget::set refuses it outright unless
; PlayerCard::IsExistId already knows it. So the strings keep their Japanese
; and the display is patched instead, the way patches/card_names.jaf does it
; for the card plate: CALLFUNC CardEnglishLabel turns the Id into its 英名 on
; the way to the label, and nothing that compares text sees anything move. The
; Id is that function's own fallback, so an entry the tree lacks -- 魔物 ストーンＧ
; is one, and reaches this panel spelled ストーンＧ, which is no card at all --
; renders as it did unpatched.
;
; A .jam for the same reason the function above is one: SetParam reads
; this.m_act on every line it draws, and the .jaf compiler resolves neither
; `this` nor a struct's own members. The body is that function verbatim from
;
;   alice ain dump -c game/ain/Rance10.v1.04.ain
;
; with two lines added and nothing else touched; regenerate it the same way if
; the game version changes, since every number in it indexes one build of one
; .ain. It adds no local, which is what makes it possible at all -- --jam
; rewrites code and leaves the FUNC section alone, so a function keeps the
; locals it was compiled with.
;
; Nothing here needs clipping. The widest of the 99 Ids that can reach this
; panel is 21 half-width units (魔物 幸福きゃんきゃん) and the widest English
; label among them is 22 (Monster Love Me Tender), so the English asks for one
; unit more than the Japanese the panel already draws. It cannot grow past that
; either: these are the card plate's own labels, and scripts/generate_card_names.js
; compresses those to the plate's 22-unit budget before they ever reach the tree.
FUNC 24857
	.STRUCTREF EnemyInformationView m_act
	PUSH 29060
	S_PUSH "Type"
	CALLMETHOD 1
	.STACK_LOCALASSIGN "<dummy : Activity@GetLabelの戻り値>"
	PUSH 29150
	S_PUSH "種族：%s"
	.GLOBALREF g_enemy
	PUSH 27699
	CALLMETHOD 0
	CALLFUNC 表示種族
	S_MOD 4
	DUP_X2
	A_REF
	CALLMETHOD 1
	DELETE
	.LOCALDELETE "<dummy : Activity@GetLabelの戻り値>"
	.STRUCTREF EnemyInformationView m_act
	PUSH 29078
	S_PUSH "Boss"
	CALLMETHOD 1
	.STACK_LOCALASSIGN "<dummy : Activity@GetPartsの戻り値>"
	PUSH 29461
	.GLOBALREF g_enemy
	PUSH 27705
	CALLMETHOD 0
	CALLMETHOD 1
	.LOCALDELETE "<dummy : Activity@GetPartsの戻り値>"
	.STRUCTREF EnemyInformationView m_act
